helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	tit				0	it	Supporto della piattaforma Java				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153089				0	it	\<link href=\"text/shared/main0650.xhp\" name=\"Supporto della piattaforma Java\"\>Supporto della piattaforma Java\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3152363				0	it	$[officename] supporta la piattaforma Java per eseguire applicazioni e componenti basati sull'architettura JavaBeans.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	it	Perché $[officename] supporti la piattaforma Java, dovete installare il software Java 2 Runtime Environment. Se i relativi file non sono già installati, viene offerta automaticamente la possibilità di installarli durante l'installazione di $[officename]. L'installazione può tuttavia essere eseguita anche successivamente.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338				0	it	Per poter eseguire le applicazioni Java dovete prima attivare il supporto della piattaforma Java in $[officename].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892				0	it	Per attivare il supporto della piattaforma Java, scegliete \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferenze\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Strumenti - Opzioni\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/java.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Java\"\>$[officename] - Java\</link\>\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id9116183				0	it	Before you can use a JDBC driver, you need to add its class path. Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - Java, and click the Class Path button. After you add the path information, restart %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0650.xhp	0	help	par_id3153822				0	it	Your modifications at the \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Java\</emph\> tab page will be used even if the Java Virtual Machine (JVM, a virtual machine for the Java platform) already has been started. After modifications to the ClassPath you must restart $[officename]. The same is true for modifications under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Internet - Proxy\</emph\>. Only the two boxes "HTTP Proxy" and "FTP Proxy" and their ports don't require a restart, they will be evaluated when you click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\main0800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	it	$[officename] e Internet				20200411 15:09:53
