helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491971				0	it	Un esempio delle differenze tra Calc ed Excel è la gestione dei valori logici. Digitate VERO nelle celle A1 e A2. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491973				0	it	In Calc, la formula =A1+A2 restituisce il valore 2, e la formula =SOMMA(A1;A2) restituisce 2. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491972				0	it	In Excel, la formula =A1+A2 restituisce 2, ma la formula =SOMMA(A1,A2) restituisce 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	it	For a detailed overview about converting documents to and from Microsoft Office format, see the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/OOoAuthors_User_Manual/Migration_Guide\"\>Migration Guide\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
