helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	it	Inserting fractions into formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	it	In the case of a fraction whose numerator and denominator consist of a product, a sum, and so on, the values that belong together must be bracketed together.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3149021				0	it	Use the following syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3083280				0	it	{a + c} over 2 = m				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	it	or				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\guide\brackets.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	it	m = {a + c} over 2				20200411 15:09:53
